                            <comment id="494087" author="sebastien" created="Wed, 6 May 2026 07:37:52 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I think this is something environmental that is causing sanity-sec test_31 to fail with &apos;unable to remount client&apos;. It started failing around 04/18, so I tried to bisect to find the patch that brought the regression, but now I can even reproduce when based on 2.16.0-ddn48, which had never shown any failure of this test at the time it was set (March 2026):&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/65678&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/65678&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=yujian&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;yujian&quot;&gt;yujian&lt;/a&gt; did you find anything on your side? I am continuing my investigations ATM.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="494106" author="gerrit" created="Wed, 6 May 2026 15:58:22 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&quot;Sebastien Buisson &amp;lt;sbuisson@ddn.com&amp;gt;&quot; uploaded a new patch: &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/65714&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/65714&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
