                            <comment id="494107" author="sebastien" created="Wed, 6 May 2026 15:58:59 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I think I managed to find the reason for these failures. sanity-sec test_31 adds a new LNet network &lt;tt&gt;${NETTYPE}999&lt;/tt&gt; to exercise the &apos;-o network&apos; mount option, so it has to also add it to &lt;tt&gt;$MGSNID&lt;/tt&gt;. But recently we started supporting Infiniband testing in Maloo, and it looks like the function &lt;tt&gt;h2name_or_ip&lt;/tt&gt; to generate a NID list for a host is not designed to filter the addresses based on the nettype currently tested. This ends up using non-existing MGS NIDs, for instance &amp;lt;the ip over ib address&amp;gt;@tcp.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I have pushed a patch to improve &lt;tt&gt;h2name_or_ip&lt;/tt&gt; and allow it to filter on the nettype being used:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/65714&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/65714&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Let&apos;s see how it goes.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="494119" author="yujian" created="Wed, 6 May 2026 19:06:51 +0000"  >&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;Jian Yu did you find anything on your side? I am continuing my investigations ATM.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Yes, &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=sebastien&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;sebastien&quot;&gt;sebastien&lt;/a&gt;. It&apos;s &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/57780&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/57780&lt;/a&gt; (&quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18637&quot; title=&quot;Control LNet network that servers use to connect to remote peers&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-18637&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18637&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; obd: add &apos;network&apos; server mount option&quot;) introducing the issue.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="494142" author="sebastien" created="Thu, 7 May 2026 06:17:14 +0000"  >&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It&apos;s &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/57780&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/57780&lt;/a&gt; (&quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18637&quot; title=&quot;Control LNet network that servers use to connect to remote peers&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-18637&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18637&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; obd: add &apos;network&apos; server mount option&quot;) introducing the issue.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I do not think so. See the fix &quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20173&quot; title=&quot;sanity-sec test_31: unable to remount client (connection timed out)&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20173&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20173&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; tests: filter on nettype when building nidlist&quot; at &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/65714&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/65714&lt;/a&gt; .&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
